# The build context is uploaded to the daemon in full before the first
# instruction runs. Anything listed here is therefore not merely excluded from
# the image - it never leaves the working directory.
#
# That matters twice over: `.cache/` holds multi-gigabyte scanner databases and
# would make every build minutes slower, and `artifacts/` holds the ephemeral
# cosign private key. A secret that is only in the context and never COPYed is
# still a secret handed to the builder, and with BuildKit's cache mounts it is
# still a secret that can end up on disk somewhere else.

.cache/
artifacts/

.git/
.github/
.gitattributes
.gitignore

# Nothing outside app/ is ever COPYed into the image; excluding it keeps the
# context small and makes an accidental COPY of the pipeline itself impossible.
deploy/
docs/
pipeline/
policies/
security/
Makefile
README.md
LICENSE
pyproject.toml

# Python and editor noise
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.idea/
.vscode/
